    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d395">

                <pb facs="0397" n="387" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg387"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.48 Refugees/4838: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in the United
                        Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bucknell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-12-08T19:00:00-04:00">December 8, 1943—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7760. Have received Algiers 106, December 7, 5 p.m. Mr. Long’s statement<anchor
                        n="60" xml:id="d395-f1"/> referred only in general way to the place of
                    temporary residence center in Africa and is not out of line with the thought in
                    the French draft.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d395-f1" n="60" xml:id="d395-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Rescue of the Jewish and Other Peoples in Nazi-Occupied
                        Territory:</hi> Hearings before the House Committee on Foreign Affairs, 78th
                    Cong., 1st sess., on H. Res. 350 and H. Res. 352 (Washington, Government
                    Printing Office, 1943), p. 15. See also <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg228">pp. 228</ref>–<ref target="#pg238">238</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
